course: dictionary
lesson: 8063
title: Relationship: how things connect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A relationship is the way two or more people, or groups, feel about and behave towards each other. It can also be the way two things are connected. «Most TV romances end after the show; real relationships take much longer than a few weeks of filming.» The clue is "take much longer", so relationships are bonds between people that grow over time.
explain: Look at the words around it: «family relationships», «a good relationship», «the relationship between». The words "between" and "family" are clues. Maths uses the word too: if one number doubles and the other doubles as well, the two numbers have a relationship. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the way two things are connected" fits.
explain: The same word can point to different kinds of link. A family relationship, such as being cousins, is a link by blood or marriage. A romantic relationship is a friendship between two people who love each other. Read the rest of the sentence to see which one the author means.
fact: A relationship is the way two or more people, or two things, are connected.
fact: «Family relationships» means how people in a family are connected, such as being cousins.
fact: «Healthy relationships» are kind, honest and respectful.
fact: A relationship can also be a romantic friendship between two people; the context tells you which meaning is used.
fact: Robin Dunbar suggested a person can keep about 150 close relationships, but the number 150 is still argued about.
exercise: «Healthy relationships» are kind, honest and respectful. What does relationship mean here? | A long journey on a train | A type of sweet | A kind of weather | *The way people feel about and behave towards each other
exercise: Which of these is a family relationship, such as being cousins? | Owning a bike | Winning a game | *Being cousins | Liking pizza
exercise: «The scientist Robin Dunbar suggested a person can keep about 150 close relationships.» What is still argued about? | The date of the sentence | The scientist's name | The colour of the book | *The number 150
test: «Real relationships take much longer than a few weeks of filming.» What does relationship mean here? | A film made in a studio | *The bonds between people that grow over time | A quick meal | A type of bicycle
test: In «the relationship between two quantities», what is connected? | A bag of sweets | *Two amounts that change together | A teacher and a class | A map of the world
exam: Mia says a relationship is only a romance. Is she right? | Yes, a relationship is always romantic | No, a relationship is only a number | *No, a relationship can also be a family connection, such as cousins | Yes, but only between grown-ups
